{"abstract":"Focusing is a known technique for reducing the number of proofs while preserving derivability. Skolemisation is another technique designed to improve proof search, which reduces the number of backtracking steps by representing dependencies on the term level and instantiate witness terms during unification at the axioms or fail with an occurs-check otherwise. Skolemisation for classical logic is well understood, but a practical skolemisation procedure for focused intuitionistic linear logic has been elusive so far. In this paper we present a focused variant of first-order intuitionistic linear logic together with a sound and complete skolemisation procedure.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bruni, Alessandro","Ritter, Eike","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798540"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Birmingham"],"keyword":["Focusing","Proof search"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"skolemisation for intuitionistic linear logic","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-63501-4_4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798540","identifier":[{"id":"85200246458","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-79f84e35-6af6-49e7-b7bc-ae4572251f58"],"keyword":["Skolemisation","first-order intuitionistic linear logic","focused intuitionistic linear logic","focusing","proof search"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-327AA5B54B65FFB70B9887EA2610B587"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-63501-4_4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-63501-4_4","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Birmingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","locid":"5c50bbc9-ed3d-417f-ba4d-e484eaf536b3","name":"Bruni, Alessandro","orcid":"0000-0003-2946-9462","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eike","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","name":"Ritter, Eike","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-63501-4_4","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"International Joint Conference on Automated Reasoning"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200246458"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-79f84e35-6af6-49e7-b7bc-ae4572251f58"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Skolemisation for Intuitionistic Linear Logic","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798540","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"For performance and verification in machine learning, new methods have recently been proposed that optimise learning systems to satisfy formally expressed logical properties. Among these methods, differentiable logics (DLs) are used to translate propositional or first-order formulae into loss functions deployed for optimisation in machine learning. At the same time, recent attempts to give programming language support for verification of neural networks showed that DLs can be used to compile verification properties to machine-learning backends. This situation is calling for stronger guarantees about the soundness of such compilers, the soundness and compositionality of DLs, and the differentiability and performance of the resulting loss functions. In this paper, we propose an approach to formalise existing DLs using the Mathematical Components library in the Coq proof assistant. Thanks to this formalisation, we are able to give uniform semantics to otherwise disparate DLs, give formal proofs to existing informal arguments, find errors in previous work, and provide formal proofs to missing conjectured properties. This work is meant as a stepping stone for the development of programming language support for verification of machine learning.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Affeldt, Reynald","Bruni, Alessandro","Komendantskaya, Ekaterina","Ślusarz, Natalia","Stark, Kathrin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730159"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Japan","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Heriot-Watt University","National Institute of Advanced Industrial Science and Technology","University of Southampton"],"keyword":["Coq Proof Assistant","Differentiable Logics","Formal verification","Machine learning","Mathematical Components"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"taming differentiable logics with coq formalisation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2403.13700","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730159","ids":["itu-0da408d4-62cf-4912-b55e-6a185253431c"],"keyword":["Coq Proof Assistant","Differentiable Logics","Formal Verification","Machine Learning","Mathematical Components"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AA9A98BBCC31819CB6A39A84FAD89D3C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.13700","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2403.13700","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"jp","key":"national institute of advanced industrial science and technology","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"National Institute of Advanced Industrial Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"heriot watt university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Heriot-Watt University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of southampton","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Southampton","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Reynald","key":"affeldtpau","last":"Affeldt","name":"Affeldt, Reynald","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","locid":"5c50bbc9-ed3d-417f-ba4d-e484eaf536b3","name":"Bruni, Alessandro","orcid":"0000-0003-2946-9462","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ekaterina","key":"komendantskayapau","last":"Komendantskaya","name":"Komendantskaya, Ekaterina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalia","key":"ślusarzpau","last":"Ślusarz","name":"Ślusarz, Natalia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kathrin","key":"starkpau","last":"Stark","name":"Stark, Kathrin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0da408d4-62cf-4912-b55e-6a185253431c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Taming Differentiable Logics with Coq Formalisation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730159","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Given how common IoT devices that use constrained resources are becoming today, the need of the hour is communication protocols which can operate securely under such limitations. For a few years, the Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF) has been working to standardize EDHOC, an authenticated key establishment protocol for such constrained IoT devices. The first version of EDHOC was proposed in 2016. In 2018, Bruni et al. [3] used the ProVerif tool [2] to formally analyze an early version of EDHOC, which had only two key establishment methods. By 2021, the protocol had been fleshed out much more, with multiple new key establishment methods, and this version was formally analyzed using the Tamarin prover [15] in [17]. In this paper, we build on that work, by modifying the model, analyzing some new properties, and discussing some aspects of the latest EDHOC specification. In particular, we extend the modeling in [17] with trusted execution environments (TEEs), modify the way we model XOR encryption, and in addition to the properties verified in [17], we verify weak post-compromise security (PCS) as well as the secrecy and integrity of some additional data used as part of the protocol.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bruni, Alessandro","Normann, Karl","Sundararajan, Vaishnavi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730198"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","University of California"],"keyword":["Authenticated key establishment","Formal verification","IoT","Protocols","Symbolic dolev yao model","Tamarin"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extended formal analysis of the edhoc protocol in tamarin","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103513496/paper_1_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-730198","identifier":[{"id":"85172422687","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-db62e580-a3e3-4e6a-bf8b-a33a2ec38a17"],"keyword":["Authenticated key establishment","Formal verification","IoT","Protocols","Symbolic dolev-yao model","Tamarin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DF7605AAE2D20785B5C45B1E7A1BC91A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103513496/paper_1_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","locid":"5c50bbc9-ed3d-417f-ba4d-e484eaf536b3","name":"Bruni, Alessandro","orcid":"0000-0003-2946-9462","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karl","key":"normannpau","last":"Normann","name":"Normann, Karl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vaishnavi","key":"sundararajanpau","last":"Sundararajan","name":"Sundararajan, Vaishnavi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-36840-0_11","eisbn":["9783031368400"],"isbn":["9783031368394"],"status":"p","title":"Extended Formal Analysis of the EDHOC Protocol in Tamarin"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85172422687"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-db62e580-a3e3-4e6a-bf8b-a33a2ec38a17"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Extended Formal Analysis of the EDHOC Protocol in Tamarin","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730198","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"A precise measurement of the curvature of the Universe is of prime importance for cosmology since it could not only confirm the paradigm of primordial inflation but also help in discriminating between different early-Universe scenarios. Recent observations, while broadly consistent with a spatially flat standard A Cold Dark Matter (ACDM) model, show tensions that still allow (and, in some cases, even suggest) a few percent deviations from a flat universe. In particular, the Planck Cosmic Microwave Background power spectra, assuming the nominal likelihood, prefer a closed universe at more than 99% confidence level. While new physics could be at play, this anomaly may be the result of an unresolved systematic error or just a statistical fluctuation. However, since positive curvature allows a larger age of the Universe, an accurate determination of the age of the oldest objects provides a smoking gun in confirming or falsifying the current flat ACDM model. (C) 2021 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.","author_count":98,"contributors":["Di Valentino, Eleonora","Anchordoqui, Luis A.","Akarsu, Ozgur","Ali-Haimoud, Yacine","Amendola, Luca","Arendse, Nikki","Asgari, Marika","Ballardini, Mario","Basilakos, Spyros","Battistelli, Elia","Benetti, Micol","Birrer, Simon","Bouchet, Francois R.","Bruni, Marco","Calabrese, Erminia","Camarena, David","Capozziello, Salvatore","Chen, Angela","Chluba, Jens","Chudaykin, Anton","Colgain, Eoin O.","Cyr-Racine, Francis-Yan","de Bernardis, Paolo","de Cruz Perez, Javier","Delabrouille, Jacques","Escamilla-Rivera, Celia","Ferte, Agnes","Finelli, Fabio","Freedman, Wendy","Frusciante, Noemi","Giusarma, Elena","Gomez-Valent, Adria","Handley, Will","Harrison, Ian","Hart, Luke","Heavens, Alan","Hildebrandt, Hendrik","Holz, Daniel","Huterer, Dragan","Ivanov, Mikhail M.","Joudaki, Shahab","Kamionkowski, Marc","Karwal, Tanvi","Knox, Lloyd","Kumar, Suresh","Lamagna, Luca","Lesgourgues, Julien","Lucca, Matteo","Marra, Valerio","Masi, Silvia","Matarrese, Sabino","Mazumdar, Arindam","Melchiorri, Alessandro","Mena, Olga","Mersini-Houghton, Laura","Miranda, Vivian","Moreno-Pulido, Cristian","Mota, David F.","Muir, Jessica","Mukherjee, Ankan","Niedermann, Florian","Notari, Alessio","Nunes, Rafael C.","Pace, Francesco","Paliathanasis, Andronikos","Palmese, Antonella","Pan, Supriya","Paoletti, Daniela","Pettorino, Valeria","Piacentini, Francesco","Poulin, Vivian","Raveri, Marco","Riess, Adam G.","Salzano, Vincenzo","Saridakis, Emmanuel N.","Sen, Anjan A.","Shafieloo, Arman","Shajib, Anowar J.","Silk, Joseph","Silvestri, Alessandra","Sloth, Martin S.","Smith, Tristan L.","Sola Peracaula, Joan","van de Bruck, Carsten","Verde, Licia","Visinelli, Luca","Wandelt, Benjamin D.","Wang, Deng","Wang, Jian-Min","Yadav, Anil K.","Yang, Weiqiang"],"cuid":["S02-098.29-043330"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, Central","America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Di Valentino, Eleonora"],"country":["Belgium","Brazil","Canada","Chile","China","France","Germany","Greece","India","Italy","Mexico","Netherlands","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Russia","South Korea","Spain","Turkey","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Academy of Athens and Nat. Observatory of Athens","All Global Affiliations","Asia Pacific Center for Theoretical Physics","Asia Pacific Center for Theoretical Physics (APCTP)","BITS Pilani, Birla Institute of Technology & Science Pilani (BITS Pilani)","Birla Institute of Technology and Science, Pilani","CCA","CEA","CNRS - The National Center for Scientific Research","California College of the Arts","California Institute of Technology","Cardiff University","Centre National de la Recherche Scientifique (CNRS)","Chinese Academy of Sciences","City University of New York","Federal University of E