{"abstract":"The IETF is standardizing an authenticated key establishment (AKE) protocol named EDHOC for constrained IoT devices. In contrast to more powerful devices like web cameras and cars, which receive a lot of media attention, such devices operate under severe energy consumption and message size restrictions. EDHOC was first formally analyzed in 2018 by Bruni et al. Since then, the protocol has been significantly extended and now has three new key establishment methods. In this paper, we formally analyze all methods of EDHOC in a symbolic Dolev-Yao model, using the Tamarin verification tool. We show that the different methods provide sensible, but also rather heterogeneous security properties, and discuss various consequences of this. Our work has also led to improvements in the design and the specification of EDHOC.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bruni, Alessandro","Normann, Karl","Sundararajan, Vaishnavi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384704"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ericsson","KTH Royal Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Authenticated Key Establishment AKE Protocol","Constrained IoT devices","EDHOC Security Analysis","Symbolic dolev yao model","Tamarin Verification Tool"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formal analysis of edhoc key establishment for constrained iot devices","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384704","ids":["itu-e8ecb3ac-f96e-469f-b990-904762a21346"],"keyword":["Authenticated Key Establishment (AKE) Protocol","Constrained IoT Devices","EDHOC Security Analysis","Symbolic Dolev-Yao Model","Tamarin Verification Tool"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8D9642FA1A04D3303BA9A4090EFA1273"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"ericsson","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Ericsson","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","locid":"5c50bbc9-ed3d-417f-ba4d-e484eaf536b3","name":"Bruni, Alessandro","orcid":"0000-0003-2946-9462","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karl","key":"normannpau","last":"Normann","name":"Normann, Karl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vaishnavi","key":"sundararajanpau","last":"Sundararajan","name":"Sundararajan, Vaishnavi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"20","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e8ecb3ac-f96e-469f-b990-904762a21346"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Formal Analysis of EDHOC Key Establishment for Constrained IoT Devices","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384704","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The current cosmological probes have provided a fantastic confirmation of the standard $\\Lambda$ Cold Dark Matter cosmological model, that has been constrained with unprecedented accuracy. However, with the increase of the experimental sensitivity a few statistically significant tensions between different independent cosmological datasets emerged. While these tensions can be in portion the result of systematic errors, the persistence after several years of accurate analysis strongly hints at cracks in the standard cosmological scenario and the need for new physics. In this Letter of Interest we will focus on the $4.4\\sigma$ tension between the Planck estimate of the Hubble constant $H_0$ and the SH0ES collaboration measurements. After showing the $H_0$ evaluations made from different teams using different methods and geometric calibrations, we will list a few interesting new physics models that could solve this tension and discuss how the next decade experiments will be crucial.","author_count":93,"contributors":["Valentino, Eleonora Di","Anchordoqui, Luis A.","Akarsu, Ozgur","Ali-Haimoud, Yacine","Amendola, Luca","Arendse, Nikki","Asgari, Marika","Ballardini, Mario","Basilakos, Spyros","Battistelli, Elia","Benetti, Micol","Birrer, Simon","Bouchet, François R.","Bruni, Marco","Calabrese, Erminia","Camarena, David","Capozziello, Salvatore","Chen, Angela","Chluba, Jens","Chudaykin, Anton","Colgáin, Eoin Ó","Cyr-Racine, Francis-Yan","Bernardis, Paolo de","Pérez, Javier de Cruz","Delabrouille, Jacques","Dunkley, Jo","Escamilla-Rivera, Celia","Ferté, Agnès","Finelli, Fabio","Freedman, Wendy","Frusciante, Noemi","Giusarma, Elena","Gómez-Valent, Adrià","Guy, Julien","Handley, Will","Harrison, Ian","Hart, Luke","Heavens, Alan","Hildebrandt, Hendrik","Holz, Daniel","Huterer, Dragan","Ivanov, Mikhail M.","Joudaki, Shahab","Kamionkowski, Marc","Karwal, Tanvi","Knox, Lloyd","Kumar, Suresh","Lamagna, Luca","Lesgourgues, Julien","Lucca, Matteo","Marra, Valerio","Ma